          "guid": "ms2x3ay27neeh9cb",
          "message": {
            "text": "The no-build app deliberately does NOT install the dev diagnostics — the served page is the production one, and that is the lesson.\n\nConsidered actually importing kerfjs/dev here so the no-build path demonstrated the same idiom as the bundled apps. Rejected: with no bundler there is no flag to fold, so an unconditional import would ship ~25 KB of dev code to every visitor of a page whose entire point is \"what you see is what runs\". Omitting the import IS the no-build production switch, which is a better thing to show than a fake dev/prod branch.\n\nThe middle ground is the importmap entry (0): mapped but never requested, so it costs nothing at runtime and a reader can enable diagnostics by adding one line instead of first discovering that the vendor copy needs another file. No change to the copy contract was required — copyNoBuildApp() already copies the whole dist/, dev.js and its chunks included.\n",
            "markdown": "The no-build app deliberately does NOT install the dev diagnostics — the served page is the production one, and that is the lesson.\n\nConsidered actually importing `kerfjs/dev` here so the no-build path demonstrated the same idiom as the bundled apps. Rejected: with no bundler there is no flag to fold, so an unconditional import would ship ~25 KB of dev code to every visitor of a page whose entire point is \"what you see is what runs\". Omitting the import IS the no-build production switch, which is a better thing to show than a fake dev/prod branch.\n\nThe middle ground is the [importmap entry](0): mapped but never requested, so it costs nothing at runtime and a reader can enable diagnostics by adding one line instead of first discovering that the vendor copy needs another file. No change to the copy contract was required — `copyNoBuildApp()` already copies the whole `dist/`, `dev.js` and its chunks included.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "site/src/examples/complete/live-poll/main.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14,
                  "endLine": 25,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "// No dev diagnostics here, on purpose: what is served IS the production app.\n// The bundled examples write `if (import.meta.env.DEV) await import('kerfjs/dev')`\n// and let the bundler fold the branch away; with no build step there is no flag\n// to fold, so here the import statement itself is the switch. Add\n//\n//   await import('kerfjs/dev');\n//\n// below while you develop — index.html's importmap already resolves it to the\n// vendored ./vendor/kerfjs/dev.js — and delete the line to ship. Put it above\n// the signals below if you want the untracked-signal warning to see them.\n\nconst OPTIONS = ["
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
